  "major": "Biology: Health Science Concentration",
  "notes": "Term-by-term curriculum as printed in the 2023-2024 ASU Undergraduate Catalog (Dept. of Biological Sciences). Prepares students for careers in health-related fields and graduate studies in nutrition, public health, health service planning and administration, health education, epidemiology, and related areas. After completing the degree plan and passing a Departmental Comprehensive (exit) Examination, the student receives the B.S. Degree in Biology with a concentration in Health Science. Students are strongly advised to take a Statistics class before FN 323, Principles of Epidemiology (catalog p.170).",
